# AI project

Agent skill: [.cursor/skills/ai-agent/SKILL.md](../skills/ai-agent/SKILL.md)

## Scope

`ai/frontend`, `ai/backend`, `ai/backend/migrations`. Website catalog widget lives under `website/frontend/src/features/ai/`.

## Ports and env

| Layer | Port | Env file |
|-------|------|----------|
| Frontend | 3020 | `ai/frontend/.env` (`VITE_*` only) |
| Backend | 4020 | `ai/backend/.env` |

Backend loads only `ai/backend/.env`. `AI_*` provider vars are **guest/bootstrap fallback** only. Signed-in users store provider/model/API key in `ai_provider_settings` via WebOnOne Basic Settings → AI (`GET/PATCH /api/v1/me/ai-settings`). Super-admin sets website guest provider via `/api/v1/admin/ai-settings`. Keys encrypted with `AI_CREDENTIALS_ENCRYPTION_KEY`.

## Auth

- Identity JWT: `iss=webonone-identity`, `aud=webonone-api`, same `JWT_SECRET`.
- Guest JWT: issued by AI (`iss=webonone-ai`) via `POST /api/v1/guest-sessions`.
- `company_id` is optional. Do not use `requireCompanyContext`.
- Owner is always from the verified token. Ignore body/query `companyId` / `userId` / `guestId`.

## Isolation

Identity: `user_id = sub AND company_id <=> jwt.companyId AND guest_id IS NULL`.
Guest: `guest_id = sub AND user_id IS NULL AND company_id IS NULL`.
Cross-principal ids return 404.

## Tools

Discover peer tools from `GET /api/v1/internal/ai/capabilities`. AI applies generic `completeCreateArgs` only. Domain schemas, palettes, and `argCompletion` live on the owning service — [ai-capabilities.mdc](ai-capabilities.mdc). Create suggestions fill **every** schema property plus related `list_*` ids; never invent IDs.

## Do not

- Put domain data in AI (tag palettes, `create_data_tag` switches, status rules, clinic/health colors).
- Let the model access MySQL, execute SQL/JS/shell, touch the filesystem, or call arbitrary URLs.
- Send JWT, API keys, or DB credentials to the provider.
- Implement login UI (Identity owns auth).
- Log secrets, tokens, or stack traces to clients.

## Verification

